Problem Statement: REST API Data Processing
You are given a REST API endpoint that returns JSON data about employees in a company. Your task is to consume this API, process the data, and produce the required output.

API Endpoint: https://jsonmock.hackerrank.com/api/employees

This endpoint returns paginated JSON data in the following format:

{
  "page": 1,
  "per_page": 10,
  "total": 50,
  "total_pages": 5,
  "data": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "name": "John Doe",
      "age": 30,
      "salary": 50000
    },
    ...
  ]
}

Task:
	Write a program that:
		Reads data from the given REST API endpoint.
		Iterates through all pages of results.
		Extracts the name of employees whose salary is greater than or equal to a given threshold.
		Prints the names in alphabetical order, one per line.

Input Format: A single integer threshold representing the minimum salary.
Output Format :
	Print the names of employees with salary ≥ threshold, sorted alphabetically.
	If no employees match, print: No Results Found

Constraints:
	1 ≤ threshold ≤ 10^6
	API may return up to 1000 employees across multiple pages.

Sample Test Cases
	Test Case 1:
		Input: 50000
		Output:
			Alice Smith
			John Doe

	Test Case 2:
		Input: 100000
		Output: No Results Found

	Test Case 3:
		Input: 75000
		Output:
			David Johnson
			Maria Lopez

	Test Case 4
		Input: 30000
		Output:
			Alice Smith
			David Johnson
			John Doe
			Maria Lopez
========================================

package com.practice.onlineTest.restapi;

import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.InputStreamReader;
import java.net.HttpURLConnection;
import java.net.URL;
import java.util.*;
import org.json.JSONArray;
import org.json.JSONObject;

public class Solution {

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int threshold = sc.nextInt();
        sc.close();

        List<String> names = new ArrayList<>();
        int page = 1;
        int totalPages;

        do {
            // Build URL with page parameter
            String apiUrl = "https://jsonmock.hackerrank.com/api/employees?page=" + page;
            URL url = new URL(apiUrl);
            HttpURLConnection conn = (HttpURLConnection) url.openConnection();
            conn.setRequestMethod("GET");

            // Read response
            BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(conn.getInputStream()));
            StringBuilder response = new StringBuilder();
            String line;
            while ((line = in.readLine()) != null) {
                response.append(line);
            }
            in.close();

            // Parse JSON
            JSONObject json = new JSONObject(response.toString());
            totalPages = json.getInt("total_pages");
            JSONArray data = json.getJSONArray("data");

            // Filter employees by salary
            for (int i = 0; i < data.length(); i++) {
                JSONObject emp = data.getJSONObject(i);
                int salary = emp.getInt("salary");
                if (salary >= threshold) {
                    names.add(emp.getString("name"));
                }
            }

            page++;
        } while (page <= totalPages);

        // Print results
        if (names.isEmpty()) {
            System.out.println("No Results Found");
        } else {
            Collections.sort(names);
            for (String name : names) {
                System.out.println(name);
            }
        }
    }
}

====================================

How It Works
	Reads the salary threshold from input.
	Calls the API endpoint with pagination (?page=1, ?page=2, …).
	Parses JSON response using org.json.
	Collects names of employees whose salary ≥ threshold.
	Sorts names alphabetically and prints them.
	Prints "No Results Found" if none match.